Z||000005||88formula||11-01-2000||05:05 PM||||I raced one with my stock Formula till about 75-mph. He got the jump off the line on me but I caught up to him till about 40mph and then he pulled a car length on me and he would have kept on pulling on me if I had not shut down. The only modification I could tell he had was one of those large exhaust tips with a performance muffler. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou_dias||11-02-2000||10:10 AM||||Back in 96 or 97, I raced a brand new 96 with a 5 speed.  I think that year it claimed 200hp.  I had my 3.3 (3.1 .060 over) and DIDN'T have my heads and intake ported or my headers and IRM exhaust yet.<BR>It was a straight strip of road 2 lanes wide.<BR>it was less than a 1/4 mile but more than 1/8 of a mile...<BR>people race hear often...  We races twice...<BR>First time, I left him at the line and easily pulled to 3 or 4 cars on him.  He claimed a bad launch so we did it again.  This time I eased it off the line and pulled 2-3 cars on him and maintained it.<P>I drove it myself later.  No torque whatsoever until 5000...but very impressive hp from 6500-7800...but by that time it's too late for the street...  VTEC is all hype...that's my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||11-02-2000||11:05 AM||||V-Tec is GREAT for road racing or cone running. but for drag cars it's jsut one more thing to fail... but its SOO fun to be in a S/C GS-R or Turbo Civic SI as the HP jumps from about 110 to 160 in 300rpm as the Vtec controller opens the solenoid! HOW SWEET! like a Fiero on Nitrous! just TOO sweet. The 3.0 CL Type S with Vtec V6 is nice.. and it'll fit in our engine bay too! so would the Alfa Quadrifoglio 3.0 out of a 164 S or LS... hummm  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||11-02-2000||11:19 AM||||the newer preludes are nice!  i wanted to buy one several years ago, but couldnt come to terms with the dealer on what they wanted to pay me for my rx7.<P>i had that car for the weekend, boy was it fun.  handled real nice, too!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||11-02-2000||03:25 PM||||My friend just turboed (greddy) his '99 Civic Si, and I tell you, its a definite sleeper.  Call it rice all you want but even without the turbo it would whip any stock fiero (with a good driver of course).<BR>It jerks you back in your seat when the V-tec kicks in and its pretty cool, but I like the torquey V8 motors better.  I like to be jerked back in my seat from the get-go....<P><BR>IMHO<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000010||Shaun41178||11-02-2000||04:42 PM||||I have never seen a newer Civic SI pull faster then a 15.9 at the track and that one was even modded with an exhaust and intake at least.  I saw this car at the Sport Compact Nationals held at Norwalk Raceway Park this past summer.   Most of the Civic Si's at the track were running mid to low 16's and I even raced one that ran a 20 second e.t.  Yea that was the drivers fault but still.  I don't think any of the mags got the Civic Si to run faster then a 15.7.<P>A Stock Civic Si vs a Stock V6 Fiero with a 4 spd would be a very close race.  It would come down to driver but I can be pretty confident that the Fiero would have it off the line and for most of the race anyways. <P>Oh yea Travis your car looks sweet! I love those rims.  Get that top secret project completed so you can go tear it up.  I wouldn't mind trying my hand at you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Later<P> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||11-02-2000||04:50 PM||||shauns right.. Si's are nice looking but not fast.. just cause its loud when the Vtec kicks in doesn't mean give up... too bad the Greddy kits not intercooled! they make such nice stuff...<P> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>i'll be happy to make a trip north when i'm done..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  you, me and Mike (Hyptno) RAISN' HELL!   thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||FIEROCIOUS||11-03-2000||03:06 AM||||My buddy has a 97 Vtec Prelude. We raced after work a month or so ago; no contest! I blew his doors off from the line on, he had no chance of catching up. About a 1/4 mile up the road I had him by 3 maybe 4 lengths. He wipped my Civic the next night though! His car is completely stock my Civic and Fiero are deffinatly not!||||reg||1
